==Awards and honors==
In 2025, Haaland was inducted into the [[Texas Trail of Fame]].<ref>[https://www.texastrailoffame.org/by-year "Texas Trail of Fame 2025"], Texastrailoffame.org.</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Bowling |first=Abbey|date=October 23, 2025 |title=Texas Trail of Fame honors 10 contributors to the American West|url=https://cw33.com/news/local/texas-trail-of-fame-honors-10-contributors-to-the-american-west/ |access-date=March 19, 2026|publisher=[[KDAF]].com}}</ref>

==Personal life==
Haaland has a child, Somáh, whom she raised as a single mother.<ref name=congress/><ref>{{Cite web |date=June 26, 2015 |title=NM Democratic Chair Haaland Statement On Marriage Equality |url=http://krwg.org/post/nm-democratic-chair-haaland-statement-marriage-equality |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180612141344/http://krwg.org/post/nm-democratic-chair-haaland-statement-marriage-equality |archive-date=June 12, 2018 |access-date=June 8, 2018 |website=KRWG}}</ref> On August 28, 2021, Haaland married her longtime partner, Skip Sayre, in [[Santa Ana Pueblo, New Mexico]].<ref>{{cite journal |date=August 29, 2021 |title=Sec. Deb Haaland Marries Long-Time Partner In Weekend Ceremony In New Mexico |url=https://abq.news/2021/08/sec-deb-haaland-marries-long-time-partner-in-weekend-ceremony-in-new-mexico/ |journal=The Paper (Albuquerque, NM) |access-date=October 11, 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=August 30, 2021 |title=Interior Secretary Deb Haaland, partner wed in New Mexico |url=https://www.sfgate.com/news/article/Interior-Secretary-Deb-Haaland-partner-wed-in-16422633.php |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210830162019/https://www.sfgate.com/news/article/Interior-Secretary-Deb-Haaland-partner-wed-in-16422633.php |archive-date=August 30, 2021 |access-date=August 30, 2021 |website=SFGATE}}</ref> She was previously married in her twenties.<ref name=":8" /> In February 2025, Haaland divorced Sayre, citing incompatibility.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Writer |first=Noah Alcala Bach / Journal Staff |date=March 13, 2025 |title=Deb Haaland divorces husband after launching campaign for governor |url=https://www.abqjournal.com/news/article_47ebf3e6-0069-11f0-952a-0313f3c77f8c.html |access-date=March 14, 2025 |website=Albuquerque Journal |language=en}}</ref>

Haaland is [[Catholic Church|Catholic]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Gstalter |first=Morgan |date=January 19, 2019 |title=Haaland condemns students' behavior toward Native elder at Indigenous Peoples March |url=https://thehill.com/blogs/blog-briefing-room/news/426160-haaland-condemns-students-behavior-toward-native-elder-at |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190404054655/https://thehill.com/blogs/blog-briefing-room/news/426160-haaland-condemns-students-behavior-toward-native-elder-at |archive-date=April 4, 2019 |access-date=April 4, 2019 |work=[[The Hill (newspaper)|The Hill]]}}</ref> Her hobbies include marathon running and gourmet cooking.<ref name="smart" />

Haaland suffered a broken left [[fibula]] on July 17, 2022, while hiking in [[Shenandoah National Park]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/07/18/deb-haaland-interior-breaks-leg/ |title=Interior Secretary Deb Haaland breaks leg while hiking in national park |date=July 18, 2022 |author1=Amy B Wang |newspaper=[[The Washington Post]] |place=Washington, D.C. |issn=0190-8286 |oclc=1330888409}}</ref>

